{
  "asyncapi": "3.0.0",
  "id": "urn:com:tradelocker:streams-api",
  "defaultContentType": "application/json",
  "info": {
    "title": "TradeLocker Streams API",
    "version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "Real-time account updates for TradeLocker accounts over [Socket.IO](https://socket.io/):\naccount status (balance, equity, margin), positions, closed positions and orders.\n\nOne Socket.IO connection carries many accounts. You connect once with your\n`developer-api-key`, then subscribe each account with a short-lived account token.\n\n## Quick start\n\n1. **Get account tokens.** `POST https://{live|demo}.tradelocker.com/backend-api/auth/jwt/accounts/tokens`\n   with the user's `email`, `password` and `server` returns one JWT per account\n   (see the `accountsTokens` channel). Do **not** send your `developer-api-key` to this endpoint.\n2. **Connect once.** Socket.IO v4 client, namespace `/streams-api`, path `/streams-api/socket.io`,\n   transport `websocket`, header `developer-api-key: <your key>`. Wait for the\n   `connection` event with `code: connected` before you subscribe.\n3. **Subscribe each account** on the same socket: emit `subscriptions` with\n   `{\"action\":\"SUBSCRIBE\",\"token\":\"<account JWT>\"}` **and an acknowledgement callback**.\n4. **Read the `stream` event.** For each account you first get a snapshot\n   (AccountStatus, Position, OpenOrder messages), then `Property` `SyncEnd`, then live updates.\n   Route messages by `brandId` + `accountId`; every message carries both.\n\n## Connection settings\n\n| Setting | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Protocol | Socket.IO v4 (Engine.IO 4) |\n| Namespace | `/streams-api` |\n| Handshake path | `/streams-api/socket.io` |\n| Transport | `websocket` only (no HTTP long-polling) |\n| Auth | header `developer-api-key` on the handshake |\n| Server ping | every 1 s, connection closed after 60 s without a pong |\n\n## Rules that save you a support ticket\n\n- **One socket, many accounts.** Do not open a socket per account. Connections per developer key\n  are capped; above the cap the handshake is rejected with `conflict`.\n- **Subscriptions belong to the socket.** When the socket closes, every subscription on it ends.\n  Socket.IO clients reconnect automatically with a *new* socket, so you must **subscribe all\n  accounts again on every `connect`**.\n- **Reconnect after a server-side close too.** Socket.IO clients retry on their own after\n  network errors and ping timeouts, but not when the server closed the connection\n  (`io server disconnect`), for example during a deploy. Reconnect yourself in that case, or every\n  account goes silent while your process looks healthy.\n- **`SyncEnd` can arrive before the subscribe acknowledgement.** Start waiting for `SyncEnd`\n  for an account *before* you emit its SUBSCRIBE.\n- **Use IDs exactly as the server sends them.** `brandId` and `accountId` are matched exactly\n  (case-sensitive). Take them from the token's `brand` and `aid` claims or from stream messages,\n  never from user input. `Blueg` is not `BLUEG`.\n- **A subscribe can take up to about 60 s** (trade-node logon plus snapshot). Give the\n  acknowledgement a timeout of at least 65 s.\n- **`Property` `Disconnected`** means that one account's stream ended. You also get it right\n  after your own UNSUBSCRIBE; any other time it ended on the server side: subscribe that\n  account again (with a fresh token if the old one has expired).\n- **Numbers are decimal strings** (`\"10628.95\"`). Parse them with a decimal type, not a float.\n  Fields with no value are omitted, not sent as `null`.\n- **Ignore message types and fields you do not know.** New ones can be added without notice.\n\nExamples in Node.js, Python, Java and C#: https://github.com/TradeLocker/streams-api-docs\n",
    "contact": {
      "name": "TradeLocker API support",
      "url": "https://github.com/TradeLocker/streams-api-docs"
    },
    "externalDocs": {
      "description": "TradeLocker REST API (orders, positions, history)",
      "url": "https://public-api.tradelocker.com/"
    },
    "tags": [
      {
        "name": "streams",
        "description": "Socket.IO events of the Streams API."
      },
      {
        "name": "auth",
        "description": "HTTP endpoint that issues account tokens for the Streams API."
      }
    ]
  },
